      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EDGAR BROMAC (1) settled close to the pace then eventually took over and kept his rivals at bay to take out a 1790m race at Mildura last start, scoring by 7 metres and recording his maiden success in the process. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this draw. It doesn't get any easier but he is good enough to take this out. KOJAX (8) was in the money two runs ago then went well again last time over 1800m at Globe Derby Park, finishing 13 metres from the winner in third. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. Has the talent to find the winners' list. MEET ME AT THE BEACH NZ (4) is one of the main contenders after winning her past three starts, the latest at Globe Derby Park a week-and-a-half ago. Difficult to ignore that sort of form. WHENIMREADY (9) found form and finished in the money two runs ago then came back to earth when he broke and finished sixth last start over 1800m at Globe Derby Park, coming home 22 metres from the winner. Each-way.",
